   "text": "the most enlightened and enterprising of the Congo communities.\" This, however, is contradicted if we consider their treatment of women. For while a semi-civilization, the civilization of the middle Congo and along the coast, brings with it stealing and lying and a low cunning, it is also accompanied, our author shows us, by an improvement in the status of women. The savagery that develops high qualities in the dominant sex reveals its inherent immorality in its treatment of all who are physically weak.",
